  "published": "2026-04-24T19:20:52.197Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.3 stable: Big bundle since 1.0.0. NEW: embedded RFC 5766 STUN/TURN server as an ASP.NET Core IHostedService (`AddRtcStunTurn(...)`). One host box can run WebSocket signaling + STUN binding + TURN relay together. Auth modes: classic long-term credentials, ephemeral/REST-API HMAC credentials (RFC 8489 §9.2 pattern a la Twilio / Cloudflare), period-rotating sub-secrets (master-secret leak only exposes currently-valid periods), tracker-gated ephemeral (only peers with live WebSocket session can allocate relays). NAT port-range support (`RelayPortRangeStart/End`) for home/SMB deployments. Origin-header allowlist (`TrackerServerOptions.AllowedOrigins`, exact + wildcard-subdomain) on the /announce WebSocket endpoint. `TrackerSignalingServer.IsPeerConnected` / `ConnectedPeerIds` / `IsOriginAllowed` exposed for consumer middleware. Tracker now completes WebSocket close-handshake cleanly and catches WebSocketException / ConnectionResetException / IOException so unclean-disconnect stack traces don't fill the fail log. Production-validated at hub.spawndev.com (full 5-step deny -> announce -> allocate -> disconnect -> deny cycle green from external client). 24 integration tests in DesktopTurnAuthTests cover every path end-to-end. See CHANGELOG.md in the repo for per-rc breakdown.",
